   "daf": "48b",
   "sentenceId": 4,
   "he": "הָיָה אָבִיו אוֹ בְּנוֹ לְתוֹכוֹ – מְשַׁלֵּם אֶת הַכּוֹפֶר. וְאַמַּאי? הָא תָּם הוּא! אָמַר רַב: בְּמוּעָד לִיפּוֹל עַל בְּנֵי אָדָם בְּבוֹרוֹת עָסְקִינַן.",
   "en": "§ The mishna teaches: If the homeowner’s «father or son were inside» the pit at the time the ox fell and the person died as a result, the owner of the ox «pays the ransom.» The Gemara asks: «But why» does he pay a ransom? «Isn’t» the ox «innocuous,» in which case its owner is not liable to pay a ransom? «Rav says:» Here «we are dealing with» an ox that is «forewarned for falling on people in pits.»"
  }
